#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:7
msgid ""
"A collaborative playbook is a checklist of the tasks that make up your "
"processes. Collaborative playbooks allow you to take codified knowledge "
"and processes and make them accessible and editable by your organization "
"and team. When you're setting up your playbook, you'll be able to break "
"tasks down, and assign actions to them - such as using a slash command to"
" start a Zoom call. You can also decide whether to use the same channel "
"every time your playbook is run, or a new one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:9
msgid ""
"There are other parts of a playbook, such as automation settings, and "
"metrics. Playbook configuration applies both to the execution of the "
"playbook as well as to its management and improvement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:11
msgid "But the very first thing you’ll want to set up is a checklist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:13
msgid ""
"Each time you use the process you’ve documented, such as onboarding a new"
" customer, the playbook is used to start a run - a discrete single use of"
" the process - and that run is captured in a channel (either a dedicated "
"one or a new one every time you run the playbook)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:15
msgid ""
"Setting up a playbook includes configuring how the playbook manages the "
"creation of its channel as well as how stakeholders are notified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:17
msgid ""
"To open a playbook and view its statistics, select the playbook name. To "
"begin a run using a specific playbook, select **Run** beside that "
"playbook’s name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:20
msgid "Templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:22
msgid ""
"Creating a playbook from scratch can be daunting, even if you have the "
"process mapped out. One way to get started quickly is to use one of the "
"pre-configured templates available. These templates are populated with "
"content and settings to provide guidance and are customizable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:24
msgid ""
"Playbook templates are basic workflows that you can use to get started "
"quickly. As you learn more about your workflows, you can customize them "
"into specific playbooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:27
msgid "Choose a template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:29
msgid ""
"The first step is to choose the right template for your use case. There "
"are pre-configured templates for specific scenarios. The checklists, "
"actions, status updates, and retrospective settings for these templates "
"may already be filled in and, where appropriate, enabled. You can always "
"edit and adjust these settings - they're there to guide you - removing "
"them doesn't negatively affect the playbook run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:33
msgid ""
"Take a look at the **Learn how to use playbooks** template. This template"
" breaks down the components of a playbook and you can also start a test "
"run to see how everything fits together. If you're taking this option, "
"you can stop reading here and enjoy the test run. You can also choose a "
"blank template and start from scratch - this is a good option if your use"
" case is unique."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:35
msgid ""
"In the incident response template, the template contains items that are "
"relevant to incident resolution. These are general items to help you get "
"started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:38
msgid "Edit a playbook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:40
msgid ""
"You can change a playbook’s configuration at any time, but changes will "
"only be applied to future incidents. Ongoing or ended incidents "
"previously started from that playbook remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:42
msgid "Go to **Product menu > Playbooks**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:43
msgid "Find the playbook you want to edit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:45
msgid ""
"Only public playbooks and private playbooks that you're a member of are "
"listed. System admins have unrestricted access to all playbooks on the "
"team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:47
msgid "Select the name of the playbook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:49
msgid ""
"To edit the playbook directly select the actions menu next to the "
"playbook name, then select **Edit**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:50
msgid "To access the playbook dashboard, select the hyperlinked playbook name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:52
msgid "Select the **Outline** tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:53
msgid ""
"Edit the text portions of the playbook inline. Use the left-hand menu to "
"navigate to other parts of the playbook that you may want to edit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:56
msgid "Make checklists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:58
msgid ""
"Checklists in a playbook or run are restricted to playbook participants "
"and owners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:60
msgid ""
"To create a checklist in a playbook, go to the **Tasks** section. Start "
"from templated tasks or create your own. Select **Add a task** or **Add a"
" section** to build out checklists in the playbook. Drag and drop to "
"reorder tasks and sections as needed. Task descriptions support a limited"
" form of Markdown, including text styling and hyperlinks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:62
msgid ""
"Playbook tasks consist of text rendered in Markdown (when present). You "
"can't run commands directly from a task in a playbook, but you can "
"trigger :doc:`built-in slash commands </integrations-guide/built-in-"
"slash-commands>` and `custom slash commands "
"<https://developers.mattermost.com/integrate/slash-commands/custom/>`_, "
"or outgoing webhooks, to run as part of the task action by starting the "
"task with ``/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:65
msgid "Channel checklists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:67
msgid ""
"From Playbooks v2.6.0, you can additionally create and manage channel-"
"based checklists directly within :ref:`public <end-user-guide/collaborate"
"/channel-types:public channels>` and :ref:`private <end-user-"
"guide/collaborate/channel-types:private channels>` channels without "
"requiring a playbook template or a run. Channel checklists use existing "
"Mattermost channel permissions to control access, so any channel member "
"who can manage channel names, headers, and purpose can create, edit, and "
"manage channel checklists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:69
msgid ""
"To create a new channel checklist or modify an existing checklist, select"
" the **Checklists** option in the top left corner of the Mattermost "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:73
msgid ""
"Channel checklists aren't available in :ref:`direct messages <end-user-"
"guide/collaborate/channel-types:direct message channels>` or :ref:`group "
"messages <end-user-guide/collaborate/channel-types:group message "
"channels>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:74
msgid ""
"To create a channel checklist, you must be a channel :ref:`Member <end-"
"user-guide/collaborate/learn-about-roles:member>` (not a :ref:`Guest "
"<end-user-guide/collaborate/learn-about-roles:guest>`). To edit a channel"
" checklist, any channel member who can post to the channel can do so, "
"including guests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:75
msgid ""
"Channel checklists in :ref:`archived <end-user-guide/collaborate/channel-"
"types:archived channels>` channels can't be modified. Archived channels "
"must be :ref:`unarchived <end-user-guide/collaborate/archive-unarchive-"
"channels:unarchive a channel>` to access and edit their channel "
"checklists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:76
msgid "A single channel can contain both playbook runs and channel checklists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:77
msgid ""
"When using Mattermost in a web browser or the Desktop app, you can "
"convert a channel checklist into a playbook by selecting the checklist "
"name and then selecting **Save as a Playbook**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:80
msgid "Multiple runs in a channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:82
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v7.7, you can choose to start each run in a new channel "
"or re-use an already existing channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:84
msgid ""
"Here are some scenarios why you might want to start each run in the same "
"channel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:86
msgid ""
"Short, frequently-used processes benefit from being in the same channel -"
" it keeps the process streamlined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:87
msgid ""
"Teams with multiple independent workflows, such as release teams, benefit"
" from having them in one place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:88
msgid ""
"Cutting down on the number of new channels created makes it easier to "
"find run channels again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:89
msgid ""
"The run name isn't linked to the channel's name so you can tell multiple "
"workflows apart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:91
msgid "When you're configuring your playbook:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:93
msgid ""
"You can link it to an existing channel so that each run starts in that "
"channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:94
msgid ""
"You can choose that each time the playbook is run, it creates a new "
"channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:96
msgid ""
"To access this setting, open the **Playbooks** tab. Select the playbook "
"you want to edit, then select the **Outline** tab. Select **Actions** in "
"the left-hand menu and make your selection under the **When a run "
"starts** heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:98
msgid ""
"When you start a run, your selection is the default but can be changed "
"for each run. Additionally, it's also possible to move a started run to "
"another channel, so you're not locked into whichever option you select."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:101
msgid "Status updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:103
msgid "There may be multiple active runs on any given day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:105
msgid ""
"Configuring an update cadence is an easy way to centralize status "
"updates, decrease noise, and remember where everything is. You can do "
"this when you're setting up your playbook. Navigate to the **Usage** "
"section and set the parameters based on expected update cycles and where "
"the updates should be published."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:108
msgid "Keywords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:110
msgid ""
"You can use keywords to trigger a playbook. Keywords are set in the "
"**Channel Actions** menu and are applicable to a specific channel. When "
"you use the Keywords action any channel member who has access to the "
"playbook and who uses one of the listed keywords will be prompted to run "
"the associated playbook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:112
msgid ""
"If you find your keywords result in too many false positives, consider "
"refining your list and also consider that URLs used by run members may "
"also contain monitored keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:115
msgid "Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:117
msgid ""
"You can customize actions associated with your playbook to ensure a "
"smooth start when starting a run. Select the **Actions** tab to view the "
"automation options available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:119
msgid "Options include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:121
msgid "Create a channel when a run is started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:122
msgid "Invite members to the run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:123
msgid "Send outgoing webhooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:124
msgid "Automatically add the run channel to a sidebar category"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:126
msgid ""
"Actions such as channel creation and adding the channel to a sidebar "
"category are set per-playbook and applied to each run that uses that "
"playbook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:128
msgid ""
"If you’re a system admin or channel admin of the run channel you can also"
" edit these settings in the run channel, via the channel menu, in "
"**Channel Actions**. Editing the settings in the run channel will only "
"affect that channel and the changes aren’t applied to the playbook. Only "
"channel admins can edit the **Channel Actions** items (such as the "
"welcome message) but members who have access to the playbook can edit the"
" welcome message and run behavior settings. Editing these won’t change "
"the welcome message of a run that’s in progress - it only applies going "
"forward. If you want to change the behavior of all future runs associated"
" with the playbook, edit the playbook directly in the **Actions** menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-playbooks.rst:131
msgid "Playbook attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/entry-ent.rst:9
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry, Enterprise, and Enterprise "
"Advanced plans <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__ (not available on "
"Professional)"
